# public/_headers — place this inside your frontend's /public folder
# Vite copies everything in /public to /dist at build time.
# Render reads _headers from the published directory root.
#
# This file is a BACKUP for the header config in render.yaml.
# Both set the same headers — having both ensures the headers apply
# regardless of which Render configuration mechanism takes precedence
# for your service type.
#
# Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
#   → Allows Google Identity Services to postMessage credentials back
#     to your page from its cross-origin popup/iframe.
#     Without this, Render's default "same-origin" COOP silently drops
#     the postMessage and Google sign-in always fails.
#
# Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: unsafe-none
#   → Disables COEP which Render may also set. COEP: require-corp would
#     block the GIS iframe from loading at all on some browsers.
#
# Cache-Control: no-store
#   → Prevents the browser from serving a stale page from bfcache
#     after logout. Without this, pressing Back after sign-out restores
#     the authenticated page from cache, bypassing ProtectedRoute.

/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: unsafe-none
  Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate
